Perfect! All tests now pass. The bug was an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was returning `parts[1]` instead of `parts[0]`, which meant it was returning the second word instead of the first word. This caused:

- `test_basic` to fail because it returned 'world' instead of 'hello'
- `test_single` to crash with an IndexError because there was no second element

The fix was simple: change `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]` to correctly return the first element of the split array.
